The attached image displays the physical characterization of Nano-11 nanoparticles, a dendrimer-like α-D-glucan vaccine adjuvant. The left panel, a Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image with a 50 nm scale bar, shows the spherical particles exhibiting an irregular, "cauliflower-like" appearance, often appearing singly or in loose pairs. The right panel presents a dynamic light scattering (DLS) histogram, illustrating the particle size distribution. It indicates a Z-average hydrodynamic diameter primarily ranging from 75 to 80 nm, confirming the uniform size of these nanoparticles which is crucial for efficient uptake by dendritic cells.